  "body": "**Description:**\r\n\r\nWith a large number of channels you can get many channels with highlighted red counts which means you were mentioned:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/187449/103490477-1de85080-4e70-11eb-97a2-b8de759b1738.png)\r\n\r\nBut there are many false positives as `@brendan` is treated identically to `@room`. A personal mention should be visually treated higher priority than a general one (we've just migrated from rocket which is how it behaves). This is tangential to how the notifications happen:\r\n\r\n* [ ]  this is a visual change to the style of the comments depending on which mention type they contain, eg personal mentions remain red, and group mentions are something less urgent, maybe blue\r\n* [ ]  and that same style should roll up to the channel indicator, so a channel which only contains group mentions will have a blue message count but any with a personal one will be red\r\n",
